.SH NAME
CWE\-294 \- Authentication Bypass by Capture\-replay
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
A capture\-replay flaw exists when the design of the product makes it possible for a malicious user to sniff network traffic and bypass authentication by replaying it to the server in question to the same effect as the original message (or with minor changes). Capture\-replay attacks are common and can be difficult to defeat without cryptography. They are a subset of network injection attacks that rely on observing previously\-sent valid commands, then changing them slightly if necessary and resending the same commands to the server.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2023\-23397
Microsoft Office, added 2023\-03\-14.
.PP
Microsoft Office Outlook Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft Office Outlook contains a privilege escalation vulnerability that allows for a NTLM Relay attack against another service to authenticate as the user.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2023\-04\-04.
.PP
